  "timingNote": "Footwork follows travel.path: drawings with a planted foot hold the box nearly still (the audit's groundSpeedPxPerMs caps it at 0.45 px/ms on screen) and the airborne drawings (dash1b, dash2, air, air2 out; skip, skipb back) carry the dash, about 28 head lengths in 115ms each way. Every cut moves the head by at most 110px and the near-hand dagger by at most 151px (about two and a half head lengths). Out: coil (sink out of the idle) 25-70, crouch 70-115, dash1 (push-off stride, box starts) 115-160, dash1b (take-off) 160-180, dash2 (flight) 180-215, air (the right arm hanging, dagger down) 215-245, air2 (arm swung forward) 245-275, dash3 (landing stride) 275-320, lunge 320-365, thrust (arm half extended) 365-410; the stab (first hit, dagger at full reach) 410-530; the rising cut with its acid-green trail (second hit) 530-585; swing1, swing2 and swing3 (the arm comes down and the dagger flips to the reverse grip) 585-720; follow-through with the cloak and scarf swinging forward 720-810. Back: rise0 and rise come up out of the stride 810-900, the skip (airborne hop back) 900-975 and skipb (descent) 975-1015 cover the trip, land 1015-1065, recover 1065-1140; the last 140ms is the exact idle drawing. Every drawing holds at least minHoldMs (45ms, so a device under 50fps never skips one) except the five flight drawings listed in shortHolds, each with its reason; the cuts keep their size and only the grounded drawings were lengthened. Both contact drawings share one dagger-tip line.",
